thesis-experiments — research-stage code (WPS locators/tries/MMPH, exact range
emptiness baselines, and competitor wrappers) split out of the main `Thesis`
product so the product stays a clean, permissively-licensed pure-Go module.

The original code in this repository is licensed under the MIT License (see
LICENSE), EXCEPT for the components noted below.

================================================================================
GPLv3 boundary — LeMonHash wrapper
================================================================================

The following Go packages are cgo wrappers that link against LeMonHash, which is
licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0:

  - locators/lemonhash
  - locators/lemon_rloc
  - locators/lemon_lerloc

LeMonHash is included as a git submodule at:

  locators/lemonhash/ext/LeMonHash

The submodule must point to a fork of https://github.com/ByteHamster/LeMonHash
that carries the local adaptations required by the cgo wrapper (static sdsl
linking, Apple-Silicon portability, std::string_view query API, debug output to
stderr). Those adaptations are recorded as a single commit on top of upstream
commit 20d8864; the same diff is archived at:

  locators/lemonhash/patches/0001-go-cgo-wrapper-adaptations.patch

Any binary produced by building or testing the packages listed above is a
combined work with LeMonHash and is therefore subject to the GPLv3. These
packages are NOT imported by the `Thesis` product, which remains GPL-free.

